        "original_id": "f844aa2d-1b9a-51d6-b6ba-d9e4392581d3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ray Stark, Stanley Kubrick, Eliot Hyman\n- Companies: Seven Arts Productions\n- Films: The World of Suzie Wong, West Side Story, The Misfits, Lolita, The Night of the Iguana, Reflections in a Golden Eye, Funny Girl, The Goodbye Girl, The Toy, Annie, Steel Magnolias, Operation Bullshine\n\nFacts:\n- Seven Arts Productions was founded in 1957 by Ray Stark and Eliot Hyman.\n- Ray Stark produced major films across the 1960s, 1970s, 1980s, and 1990s after a background as a literary and theatrical agent.\n- Ray Stark's produced films included The World of Suzie Wong, West Side Story, and The Misfits in 1961.\n- Stanley Kubrick directed Lolita, a 1962 British-American black comedy-drama film.\n- Ray Stark's produced films included Lolita in 1962 and The Night of the Iguana in 1964.\n- Seven Arts Productions released Operation Bullshine in the USA in 1963.\n- Ray Stark's produced films included Reflections in a Golden Eye in 1967, Funny Girl in 1968, The Goodbye Girl in 1977, The Toy and Annie in 1982, and Steel Magnolias in 1989.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6b61de0c-66f9-52b7-af77-da21b572145a",
        "text": "Page: Ray Stark. Sentence: Highly tenacious and intelligent, Stark’s background as a literary and theatrical agent groomed him to produce some of the most dynamic and profitable films of the 1960s, 1970s, 1980s, and 1990s, such as \"The World of Suzie Wong\" (1961), \"West Side Story\" (1961), \"The Misfits\" (1961), \"Lolita\" (1962), \"The Night of The Iguana\" (1964), \"Reflections in a Golden Eye\" (1967), \"Funny Girl\" (1968), \"The Goodbye Girl\" (1977), \"The Toy\" (1982), \"Annie\" (1982), and \"Steel Magnolias\" (1989).\nPage: Lolita (1962 film). Sentence: Lolita is a 1962 British-American black comedy-drama film directed by Stanley Kubrick.\nPage: Seven Arts Productions. Sentence: It was founded in 1957 by Ray Stark and Eliot Hyman.\nPage: Operation Bullshine. Sentence: The film was released in the USA in 1963 by Seven Arts Productions.",
